1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:25,160
 The Free Software Foundation's mission is to promote users' freedom to copy and redistribute

2
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:27,180
 and change software.

3
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:30,040
 Free software refers to freedom, not price.

4
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:36,640
 So the alternative to free software is proprietary software, proprietary software that subjugates

5
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,440
 and divides the users.

6
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:39,560
 That's what's wrong about it.

7
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:41,420
 It's because it divides and subjugates people.

8
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:43,960
 It doesn't respect users' freedom.

9
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:48,040
 It doesn't allow users to be part of a community, and that's why it's wrong.

10
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:51,880
 It's not wrong for programmers to make money, and as long as they can make money in a way

11
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:55,160
 that respects the freedom of other people, I think that's good.

12
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:59,720
 After all, I'm a programmer, and I'm not unhappy when I make some money, but I only do it in

13
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:02,200
 ways that respect the freedom of other people.

14
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:08,560
 Back in the 1980s, it was possible for people to speculate, speculatively assume that we

15
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:13,320
 couldn't possibly do such a big job because nobody would write the software if they weren't

16
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:14,320
 getting paid.

17
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:18,880
 Well, now we know from experience that lots of people will work on free software even

18
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:23,440
 if they don't get paid, and at the same time, a number of people have found ways to get

19
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:30,380
 paid to write free software, so we've now shown that we can do very large jobs.

20
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:36,200
 We can produce a broad spectrum of software that is very high quality and that users like

21
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:37,200
 to use.

22
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:41,960
 Well, I think that the World Wide Web should eventually become the free encyclopedia of

23
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:46,280
 all knowledge, that it should have articles covering every topic that you'd want to have

24
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:52,880
 in an encyclopedia, and every one of these articles should be available for access at

25
00:01:52,880 --> 00:02:00,560
 no charge, and that people should be permitted to redistribute them also, and also to quote

26
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:04,840
 parts, any part of the article in a new article.

27
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:10,280
 I think that they'll be written mostly by teachers, college teachers, high school teachers.

28
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:16,900
 You know, if each one writes an article a year, if each, say, not every teacher, because

29
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:21,540
 obviously they won't all do this, but if a couple of thousand teachers get involved and

30
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:26,400
 each one writes an article per year, that's not a very large part of your time, and that'll

31
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:28,300
 get the job done in a decade or two.

